      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "RFC: Claws",
        "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\nAdds an RFC for **Claws**: versioned starter setup manifests for OpenClaw agents. A Claw can compose skills, plugins, MCP servers, connectors, workspace files, persona files such as `SOUL.md`, heartbeat/crons, schedules, and automations into one inspectable setup flow.\r\n\r\n## Motivation\r\n\r\nOpenClaw has skills, plugins, compatible bundles, package sources, and hosted feeds, but not a focused way to describe a governed scenario-level starter setup that can be inspected, planned, applied, updated, disabled, and explained later through provenance.\r\n\r\n## Current shape\r\n\r\n- Uses `Claw` / `Claws` for the user-facing concept and `claw` for schema/feed/CLI kinds.\r\n- References RFC 0009 as the feed dependency: feeds provide discovery, curation, approval, block, pin, deprecation, and effective-view resolution.\r\n- Keeps Claws distinct from packages, plugin-bundled skills, compatible bundles, prior Agent Pack/workspace-template proposals, and whole-agent export/import.\r\n- States the safety guarantee up front: no silent workspace mutation, no silent automation enablement, and no transitive approval of Claw members.\r\n- Defines typed entries, read-only planning, dry-run apply plans, plan/provenance JSON shapes, workspace-file safety, automation safety, compatibility/migration, and acceptance criteria.\r\n- Treats `apply` as the Claw lifecycle verb; artifact install is one possible phase inside a later mutating apply.\r\n\r\n## PR sequencing\r\n\r\nInitial OpenClaw validation track (one RFC PR plus five OpenClaw implementation PRs):\r\n\r\n1. RFC and terminology.\r\n2. Schema, local reader, inspect, and read-only plan.\r\n3. Feed integration and read-only feed planning.\r\n4. Artifact and provenance preview.\r\n5. Dry-run apply lifecycle.\r\n6. Lifecycle CLI E2E proof.\r\n\r\nFuture OpenClaw mutating track, after maintainer acceptance:\r\n\r\n- Artifact apply and provenance persistence.\r\n- Workspace file and persona apply.\r\n- Automation enablement.\r\n- Status, update, remove, and rollback.\r\n\r\nClawHub track, dependent on stable OpenClaw schema/parser fixtures and plan/apply-plan JSON:\r\n\r\n1. Schema ingestion and data model.\r\n2. Publish validation and authoring docs.\r\n3. Search, detail, and API surfaces.\r\n4. Feed export and published E2E.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\nCurrent head: `1b80d1b74bdaf8ba116ac7c4b98601bed54d7cfb`\r\n\r\n```text\r\n$ git diff --check HEAD^..HEAD\r\n# no output\r\n\r\n$ Select-String -Path rfcs\\0016-claws.md -Pattern \"install plan|claws install|claws uninstall|six OpenClaw|first complete OpenClaw|plan/install/status|read-only plan JSON|clawInstall|installedAt\" -Context 1,1\r\n# no output\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n",
